    <!-- HERO BANNER -->
    <header class="about-hero">
      <div class="container reveal">
        <h1>The Man Behind the Workshop</h1>
        <p>Five decades of craftsmanship, precision, and passion for restoration.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- TONY'S STORY -->
    <section class="section container">
      <div class="split-layout">
        <div class="reveal">
          <img src="images/about-tony.jpg" alt="Tony Warden — Master Craftsman" class="rounded-image shadow" />
        </div>
        <div class="reveal about-text">
          <div class="section-title left-align">
            <h2>Master Craftsmanship Since 1976</h2>
            <div class="underline"></div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Tony Warden has spent over five decades turning broken, worn, and forgotten
            things into objects of beauty and function. What began as a childhood
            fascination with how things work — taken apart and reassembled with careful
            hands — grew into a lifelong vocation.
          </p>
          <p>
            In 1976, Tony formalized that passion into Warden's Workshop, a name that has
            since become synonymous with quality and dependability throughout Essex County
            and surrounding Ontario communities.
          </p>
          <p>
            Whether he is bringing a century-old sewing machine back to life,
            weatherproofing an RV for another season on the road, or transforming a dated
            living space into something a homeowner can be proud of, Tony approaches every
            project with the same discipline: obsessive care and surgical precision.
          </p>
          <p><strong>No shortcuts. No compromises. Just craftsmanship.</strong></p>
          <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: 25px">Get a Free Estimate</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TIMELINE -->
    <section class="section bg-warm">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-title text-center reveal">
          <h2>A Legacy Built Over Decades</h2>
          <div class="underline"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="timeline reveal">

          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">1976</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <h3>The Workshop Begins</h3>
              <p>Tony establishes Warden's Workshop, taking on his first restoration projects in Essex, ON — primarily vintage mechanical repairs and furniture restoration.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">1980s</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <h3>Expanding into Home Services</h3>
              <p>Growing demand from satisfied customers leads Tony into interior and exterior painting, as well as light home renovation work throughout Essex County.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">1990s</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <h3>RV Revitalization Specialty</h3>
              <p>Tony develops a reputation for comprehensive RV restoration — structural repairs, interior remodeling, and weatherproofing — becoming a trusted name in the regional RV community.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">2000s</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <h3>Technical Mastery Recognized</h3>
              <p>Word spreads about Tony's ability to restore vintage sewing machines and antique mechanisms that others have given up on. Clients travel from across Ontario seeking his technical expertise.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="timeline-item">
            <div class="timeline-year">Today</div>
            <div class="timeline-body">
              <h3>50 Years Strong</h3>
              <p>Warden's Workshop continues to serve Essex and surrounding communities with the same dedication that started it all — one project at a time, done right.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- VALUES -->
    <section class="section container">
      <div class="section-title text-center reveal">
        <h2>What We Stand For</h2>
        <div class="underline"></div>
        <p class="subtitle">The principles that guide every project Tony takes on.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="values-grid">

        <div class="value-card reveal">
          <i class="fas fa-medal"></i>
          <h3>Uncompromising Quality</h3>
          <p>Every project is finished to the same standard — the one Tony would apply if the work were his own home, his own heirloom.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="value-card reveal">
          <i class="fas fa-history"></i>
          <h3>Respect for History</h3>
          <p>We don't just repair things. We honor the story behind them — whether that's a machine built in 1920 or a family home built in 1960.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="value-card reveal">
          <i class="fas fa-handshake"></i>
          <h3>Honest Dealing</h3>
          <p>Straightforward assessments, transparent pricing, and a commitment to only taking work we are certain we can deliver on.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="value-card reveal">
          <i class="fas fa-tools"></i>
          <h3>Hands-On Precision</h3>
          <p>Tony is not a manager who delegates. He is the craftsman who shows up, rolls up his sleeves, and sees the job through personally.</p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="section bg-dark text-white text-center">
      <div class="container reveal">
        <h2>Ready to Start a Project?</h2>
        <p style="opacity: 0.8; margin: 20px 0 35px; font-size: 1.1rem;">Tell Tony what you need. Every project starts with a conversation.</p>
        <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-primary">Get a Free Estimate</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer>
